From: lws-hmi <devnull@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] softvol: skip AVRCP Absolute Volume sync on A2DP Sink

When SoftVolume is enabled, upstream already skips MediaTransport Volume
writes for A2DP Source / HF AG. For A2DP Sink, bluealsa still pushes volume
to BlueZ; on AIC8800 that fails with ENOENT and spam:
  bluetoothd: set_volume() Unable to set volume: No such file or directory (-2)
  bluealsa: Couldn't set BT device volume: ... Failed ...

Soft-volume scaling still works locally (HMI + phone Absolute Volume via
PropertyChanged). Skip the broken Sink→AVRCP write.

---
 src/ba-transport.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ba-transport.c b/src/ba-transport.c
--- a/src/ba-transport.c
+++ b/src/ba-transport.c
@@ -1744,11 +1744,14 @@
 
 	struct ba_transport *t = pcm->t;
 
-	/* In case of A2DP Source or HSP/HFP Audio Gateway skip notifying Bluetooth
-	 * device if we are using software volume control. This will prevent volume
-	 * double scaling - firstly by us and then by Bluetooth headset/speaker. */
+	/* Skip notifying Bluetooth Absolute Volume when using software volume.
+	 * Upstream only skipped A2DP Source / AG; as A2DP Sink we also skip — on
+	 * AIC8800, MediaTransport Volume → avrcp_set_volume returns ENOENT and
+	 * floods journal while soft-volume already works. */
 	if (pcm->soft_volume && t->profile & (
-				BA_TRANSPORT_PROFILE_A2DP_SOURCE | BA_TRANSPORT_PROFILE_MASK_AG))
+				BA_TRANSPORT_PROFILE_A2DP_SOURCE |
+				BA_TRANSPORT_PROFILE_A2DP_SINK |
+				BA_TRANSPORT_PROFILE_MASK_AG))
 		goto final;
 
 	if (t->profile & BA_TRANSPORT_PROFILE_MASK_A2DP) {
